libfvad is itself an extraction of the voice-activity-detection component
from the WebRTC project's legacy GMM VAD (webrtc/common_audio/vad and
webrtc/common_audio/signal_processing), repackaged as a small standalone
library with no other WebRTC dependencies. It is pure fixed-point integer
arithmetic (no float/double anywhere in the VAD path), so the Go port in
vad/internal/fvad is bit-exact with no floating-point build-tag ceremony.

Compiled ONLY by the parity_tests cgo slices (vad/internal/parity_tests/
fvad_sp, fvad_filterbank, fvad_gmm, fvad_core, fvad_e2e) — no root cgo
bridge, mirroring the loudness/libebur128 and libraries/flac/libflac
vendoring pattern.

